[/asy]

solution_steps:
Let the three integers be $a,$ $b,$ and $c$.
We can write the given information as:
\begin{align*}
a &\equiv 10 \pmod{24} \\
b &\equiv 4 \pmod{24} \\
c &\equiv 12 \pmod{24}
\end{align*}
Adding these congruences, we have:
\begin{align*}
a + b + c &\equiv 10 + 4 + 12 \pmod{24} \\
a + b + c &\equiv 26 \pmod{24}
\end{align*}
Since $26 \equiv 2 \pmod{24}$, the remainder when the sum of the three integers is divided by $24$ is $\boxed{2}$.The answer is: 2

